# City Brush round lm40 — Singapore: 96 NEW landmark / site targets in 8 groups (sg40a … sg40h), to take Singapore past 200.
# Same contract as lm26/targets_sg.py: TARGETS[group] = [(key, name, lat, lon, ref_radius_m)], read by lm40/s40_refs.py.
# T40 carries the rest for the model authors and the integrator:
#   key, zh (Simplified), en, kind ('landmark' | 'site'), lat, lon (centroid of the real footprint in the app's data unless
#   'anchor' says otherwise), r (suggested model radius m; refs use RR = max(r*1.6, r+60)), osm (OSM way/relation of the footprint
#   the anchor sits on: w… / r…; 'line' = a road/path line (no ids kept for roads); '-' = POI only), h (verified overall height m,
#   None = not verified), hs (source of h / key facts), note (what makes it recognisable), unc (None, or why the anchor is uncertain).
# Data heights in the refs are OSM / estimates and often wrong for towers (e.g. Capital Tower 172.8 in the data vs 254 real).
# Only what 'hs' lists was checked this round; years / architects / features in 'note' beyond 'hs' are recognition hints to verify.
# Existence checked: every anchor sits on a footprint / POI / line of the current data; demolished or replaced places were left out
# (old Sentosa Merlion, Jurong Bird Park); S.E.A. Aquarium is now the Singapore Oceanarium (Jul 2025); Mandarin Orchard is now
# Hilton Singapore Orchard (Feb 2022); the Chinese & Japanese Gardens reopened Sep 2024; TreeTop Walk reopened Dec 2021.
# Left out because already modelled: Customs House (in 'cliffordpier'), Sri Krishnan Temple (in 'sgkwanim'), Read Bridge (in
# 'sgclarkequay'). Left out for lack of a placeable footprint: SGH Bowyer Block, the cable-car Tower 2, Kusu Island temple.
